sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/reference/tasks.md#prepare-a-command, the Gateway side of stage 1 of the command development pipeline (docs/reference/pipeline/1-prep.mmd). The pattern of proof:run: one admission, one parent Swamp run, existing workflows as children.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: task:prep
  %% kind: tasks.prep
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=terminal pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>author · reviewer
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>draft PR
  CLI->>GW: task:prep 42<br/>command firewall:deny
  %%> Command:
  %%> - the MCP tool `task-prep`, or `POST /api/v1/tasks/42/prep` with `{"command": "firewall:deny"}` and an `Idempotency-Key`
  Note over GW: Admit one prep run<br/>group 42 · capture the intent
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway
  %%> - group 42 is an open external `todo` group with no VM, of a Project that the GitHub App reads
  %%> - the command is `family:command` in lower case
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - captures, in one transaction, the provision intent, the author and reviewer threads, the prompts, the pull request title and body, and the repository, base and branch `task-42`, and the review mode of the group (`manual` or `automatic`)
  %%> - names the vault keys of the push token; it mints no GitHub token, because the run takes longer than the hour that an installation token lives
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Operation recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start one run, full intent<br/>operation-task-prep
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the whole intent above, and the vault key names of the model, Pi and push-token credentials, never their values
  %%> - two steps of the run mint a GitHub credential at the Gateway, with the run id of this run: the clone step of the provision child and the publish step
  %%> - no task VM holds a GitHub credential: it receives the workspace in the provision bundle, and the push and the pull request run on Node 209
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation recorded
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the Operation with `operation:show`
  SW->>VM: Create the VM<br/>operation-task-provision
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs the provision workflow as a child, with its intent from the parent's inputs
  %%> - the VM, the workspace and the checkout of the default branch
  %%> - the host key of the new VM is unknown at admission; a step pins it into the SSH targets of the later children
  SW->>VM: Draft the spec<br/>operation-task-turn
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the author agent drafts the chart, the page and the cases, checks them (including the runner plan of the cases file), and commits the three files as one commit
  %%> - the turn reports the commit and tree it left
  alt the draft moved HEAD
    loop until the review has no findings, at most 3 rounds
      SW->>VM: Plan the cases<br/>runner.py plan
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - runs `python3 swamp/proof/runner/runner.py plan --file` on the cases file as one `@swamp/ssh exec` with literal arguments; exit 0 and 3 are accepted
      %%> - runs after the draft and after each fix; the Gateway captured the path of the cases file at admission
      %%> Result:
      %%> - a refusal (exit 3) is added to the findings of the round, so the review cannot approve past it and the fix turn gets it
      SW->>VM: Review the spec<br/>operation-task-turn
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - a new reviewer thread restores the commit under review and reads the spec
      %%> - its receipt is `approved` or `changes_requested` with the findings
      VM-->>SW: Findings or none
      SW->>VM: Fix the findings<br/>operation-task-turn
      %%> When:
      %%> - only when the review has findings
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the author thread fixes them and commits again
    end
    alt the last review has no findings
      SW->>GW: Mint the push token<br/>operation:direct:github-token
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the publish child asks for the token only now, right before the push
      SW->>GH: Open a draft PR<br/>operation-task-publish
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - pushes the commit to `task-42` without force and opens the PR as the Orbit App, as a draft
      SW-->>GW: Native terminal result<br/>PR number · URL · commit
      Note over GW: Record the draft PR<br/>PR · subtask done
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the group keeps its VM; the pull request fields of the group are set for stage 4
      %%> - the spec subtask of the group is marked completed, so the group has no open subtask
      %%> - in manual mode (the review mode of the group at admission), the Gateway then admits `task:park` for the group, which stops the VM while the spec waits for the owner; a refused park is kept in the result as `park_refused`
      %%> - in automatic mode it parks nothing, and the VM keeps running
      %%> Why:
      %%> - `task:park` refuses a group with an open subtask; with the subtask completed it can stop the VM while the spec waits for review, and the workspace stays
      %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
      %%> - prep completes its subtask when the App opens the draft PR; park keeps its rule that no subtask is open
      %%> - the park follows the mode and needs no step in the run, like the park after `task:prep-fix`
    else findings are left
      SW--xGW: Native failed result<br/>tasks.prep_review_unresolved
      %%> Result:
      %%> - nothing is published; the VM stays for the orchestrator
    end
  else HEAD did not move
    SW--xGW: Native failed result<br/>tasks.prep_not_committed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no review runs; the VM stays for the orchestrator
  end
  loop until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show<br/>Operation number
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Operation status, and the pull request when the run succeeded
  end
